WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Republicans are standing
in the way

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.504
of urgently needed action

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.207
to take on the real world
effects of climate change,

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.943
even after the destruction
wrought by Hurricane Ida

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:13.413
and at the same time,
they´re also staging a stunning

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
and brazen attack on
Roe v. Wade with the help

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
of conservatives
on the Supreme Court.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
For more on this,
it´s time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, last week was
a real bad news parade

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were off,
which means

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn´t have
the catharsis of the show

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:31.765 size:84% position:42%
to vent all my outrage,
making matters worse,

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spent the week at my least
favorite place on earth,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
the beach, where not only
was I hot and sandy,

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.271
but my kids were giving me hell

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.939
because I didn´t bring
the right plastic shovels

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
they liked.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like,
what´s wrong with this shovel?

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
we like the green ones.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, well,
I like staying inside

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doing the "New York Times"
spelling bee,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we don´t always get
what we want.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they said,
you´re stupid.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.052
And I said, stupid, actually,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
three out of seven days,
I´m a genius.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I´m not,
it´s because of some dumbass

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
not a word pangram
like jouncing.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.160
Anyway, and these days,
you don´t have to look very far

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
for bad news.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.463
Here in New York City,
the destruction of Hurricane Ida

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
was so bad, they were
practically rivers pouring

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.803
into people´s homes and cars
floating in five feet of water.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
The flooding was so bad
the subway

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.206
looked like a white water rapid.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was waiting for an F train
and instead,

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.644 size:84% position:42%
an MTA canoe pulled up,

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
and even that had a guy
with a bike taking up space.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.483
It´s undeniable,
as it has been for a long time,

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
that climate change
is intensifying these storms

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
and having deadly
real world impacts right now,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we can see in front of us
with our own eyes,

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
much of the West
has been on fire this summer.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wildfire smoke has drifted
all the way across the country

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and made the air toxic on
the East Coast.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And New York City
just had to declare its first

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.633
ever flash flood emergency.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s getting so bad
that pizza rat

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.537
has taken up water ballet,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I hope, I just hope,
it waited a half hour

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
after eating.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.779 size:81% position:41%
He looks great because
he ate a lot of pizza

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.614
and he didn´t look great,
but now he´s swimming.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
He looks great.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, as they were airing
a press conference

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
with local officials
discussing storm damage,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:05.191 size:81% position:41%
the supposed news side
of Fox News cut away

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.093
and dismissed any discussion

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
of climate change as quote,
"political."

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:12.432
-Because of climate change
and these record storms,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:17.737 size:84% position:42%
storms that were once
in 500 years, I´m told.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now that we´ve got
a look at them to be storms

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:26.212
that come in a regular manner
more intense, as indicated.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:31.417
And so I want to thank --
I spoke to Speaker Pelosi

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:35.555
to make sure that we work very
closely with Senator Schumer.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.558
So there´s no separation between
the House and the Senate.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.394
And I think all of the members
of the United States Congress

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:45.632
and bringing the resources here
to the City of New York.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me thank the mayor
and the governor

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
for their working
on this instantaneously.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This has turned politically
quite quickly.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
It didn´t take long to put
the focus on

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
"climate change."

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s Fox,
quote unquote news.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:06.452
We´re way past the quote unquote
part of climate change.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.921 size:78% position:39%
Americans are dealing
with unprecedented

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.957
flooding and deadly wildfires
intensified by climate change,

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:14.394
and you guys sounds like parents
trying to understand TikTok.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.929
My kids keep filming themselves

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
singing sea shanties
in their bedroom.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess they´re trying
to go quote unquote viral,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it´s not just these
anti-science reactionaries

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.937 size:88% position:44%
we have to contend with.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are also the so-called
moderate Democrats

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
standing in the way
of major climate legislation

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
like West Virginia
Senator Joe Manchin,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
who recently announced that
he won´t support the Democrats

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.682
$3.5 trillion spending bill that
contains, among other things,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
significant investments
in climate infrastructure.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Moderate Democrat Senator
Joe Manchin

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:44.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
is urging fellow Democrats
to hit the pause button

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
on that $3.5 trillion
spending bill,

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.596 size:78% position:39%
saying there are more
urgent priorities.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.764
-Manchin in the past has already
raised concerns

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.032 size:75% position:38%
about the price tag,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
but now he is raising concerns
about the timing,

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.704
and that could throw the wrench
in this process

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
and could upend efforts
to pass this,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as a separate
$1.2 trillion

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.277 size:75% position:38%
infrastructure plan.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just moments ago,
he wrote in an op-ed

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.848
in "The Wall Street Journal,"
instead of rushing to spend

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
trillions
on new government programs

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
and additional
stimulus funding,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congress should hit
a strategic pause.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First of all, what would
a pause look like

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Capitol Hill, a place where
it takes longer to pass

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.594
a single piece of legislation

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.496
than it takes to get
a third season of "Succession"?

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
And don´t get me wrong,
I cannot wait

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a new season of
"Succession."

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:31.170
I just worry when Logan Roy
has more time to scheme.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dad?

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.610
Second, you want to pause
on legislation that would,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
among other things,
expand health care

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
amid a once-in-a-century
pandemic,

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
invest in job
creating infrastructure

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.419
amid an unemployment crisis,
and address climate change

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
amid unprecedented
floods and fires?

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:51.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
You really think now
is the time for a pause?

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re like the guy
in the zombie movie

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.228
who thinks everyone should stop
running toward the military base

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
and instead just hide out
in the shed.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.132 size:78% position:39%
Guys, I know zombies.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re not going to come
into the shed.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now which one of you
is shuffling and moaning?

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:07.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no! I´m sorry,
you don´t get to take a pause

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.574
when the stakes are this high.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:11.144
Although I guess you don´t have
to worry about rising sea levels

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.812
when your house is a boat.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.347 size:88% position:44%
-Your profile of Manchin

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
it´s got a lot of really
interesting details.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.417
Not the least of which
is that the senator lives

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the Potomac River
in a houseboat

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
named after
a John Denver lyric.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Back in March,

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ron Klain, the chief of staff
of the White House,

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
went to dinner
with Joe Manchin.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.959 size:81% position:41%
One thing I discovered
during the reporting

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
went to visit him
on that houseboat.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had dinner,
and during the dinner,

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Biden called
and said,

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.233 size:81% position:41%
you know, when are you
inviting me out there?

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why does the senator
have a houseboat?

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
Houseboats are for cops
who play by their own rules

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
and drink whiskey
from the bottle

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.175
while looking at a framed photo
of their ex-wife.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.744 size:81% position:41%
Oh, sure, she´s with
that fancy lawyer now,

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I bet she still thinks
about you all the time.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
God, you guys sure
had some good times.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, oh, you fought like
cats and dogs.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:54.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
But damnit, she could
always find the pangram.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.423
You jounce my heart, Sheila.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, Lindsey Graham
was reportedly on the boat

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:02.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
before he was diagnosed
with COVID and COVID aside,

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can´t think of anything
less appealing

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.099
than being trapped on
a houseboat with Lindsey Graham.

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:09.268
If you ever find my body
floating in the East River,

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.603
It was one or two things.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
Either the mob
put a hit out on me

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
for making too many jokes
about the Mets,

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
or I was on a houseboat
with Lindsey Graham

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
and swimming home
was the only other option.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where are you going?
I was just about

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.815
to crack open a sarsaparilla
and tell you about the time

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.818 size:84% position:42%
I was voted most polite
at the Meemaw Awards.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s an award voted on
and presented by my meemaw.

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:31.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
I usually sweep
the major categories.

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
Splash!

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:37.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
The nation faces a series
of massive existential crises

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
brewing all at once,
and we can´t just sit around

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
and wait for one guy
in a houseboat

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.871
to decide whether he wants
to do something about it.

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.874
Whether it´s the pandemic,
climate change, democracy itself

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the right´s intensifying
assault on Roe v. Wade,

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
which took
a horrifying turn last week

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:54.747 size:81% position:41%
when the Supreme Court
in the dead of night

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:58.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
upheld a heinous and truly
diabolical law in Texas

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
that bans abortions
in brazen defiance

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Supreme Court precedent
and the Constitution.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.223 size:81% position:41%
-In the dead of night,

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
they did it
in the dead of night,

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
five Republican Supreme
Court justices,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
including three appointed
by Donald Trump,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:12.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
a man who lost
the popular vote in 2016

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.734
by nearly three million votes.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.236 size:88% position:44%
They destroyed a woman´s
right to bodily autonomy

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.671 size:88% position:44%
and reproductive choice.

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:22.308
First in the state of Texas,
but who knows what´s next?

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they did it shortly
before midnight.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
No big public announcement
with an order

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is barely more
than a page long.

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.818
-That´s right, they did it
in the dead of the night

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:32.919
in little more than a page.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
The same way a rich kid
half asses

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.955 size:88% position:44%
a freshman English paper

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he knows he can´t
fail out.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.158 size:75% position:38%
The font is size 16.

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:41.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
The margins are two inches
on each side,

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:46.265
and at one point you claim
"Beowulf is about a wolf

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
"who lives by the bay
on a houseboat like my dad

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
the senator."

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:56.476
A-minus?
Also, three of the five justices

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.511 size:84% position:42%
who wrote this odious
and contemptuous ruling

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:01.314
were appointed by a deeply
unpopular one-term president

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
who lost the popular vote
by three million.

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
They gutted a woman´s
right to choose in Texas,

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.154
and who knows where else next

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
despite never
commanding majority support

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:11.958
from the American people,

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:13.526
And they don´t give a [bleep]
because they´re there for life.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:15.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if that´s how our
government is going to work,

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
